From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msctf: context notifications, views, edit records and ranges

A Text Services Framework context did not pass on what its text store
told it -- OnTextChange, OnSelectionChange and OnLayoutChange were
"STUB"s, OnAttrsChange and the edit transaction calls returned E_NOTIMPL
-- and accepted only text edit sinks; its views (GetActiveView,
EnumViews), InWriteSession and almost all of ITfRange were E_NOTIMPL. Text
services and accessibility tools that follow an editor's text and caret
got nothing, and an edit record was always NULL.

- The context takes the layout, status, edit transaction and context key
  event sinks (AdviseSink), and tells them: OnLayoutChange (with the view),
  OnStatusChange, OnStartEditTransaction/OnEndEditTransaction.
- Text and selection changes the text store reports outside an edit
  session are told to the text edit sinks under a read lock, with an
  ITfEditRecord: whether the selection changed, and the changed text as a
  range (GetTextAndPropertyUpdates). Edit sessions' OnEndEdit gets a
  record too. A read lock with nothing changed tells nobody, as before.
- The context's view (ITfContextView: GetRangeFromPoint, GetTextExt,
  GetScreenExt, GetWnd -- the text store's view answers), GetActiveView,
  EnumViews (the one view), and InWriteSession (the client is in a
  read/write session of the context now).
- ITfRange: GetText (TF_TF_MOVESTART, TF_TF_IGNOREEND), SetText (the
  range then covers the new text), GetFormattedText, GetEmbedded,
  InsertEmbedded, ShiftStart/ShiftEnd within the document,
  ShiftStartToRange/ShiftEndToRange, ShiftStartRegion/ShiftEndRegion (no
  regions), IsEmpty, IsEqualStart/IsEqualEnd, CompareStart/CompareEnd,
  AdjustForInsert (QueryInsert), Get/SetGravity, Clone, and ITfRangeACP's
  GetExtent/SetExtent.
- msctf.idl gains ITfTextLayoutSink, ITfStatusSink,
  ITfEditTransactionSink, ITfContextKeyEventSink and TfLayoutCode.

Wine's msctf inputprocessor tests: 285 tests, no failures, as before.

Gate: test/tsfsinks-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/tsfsinks-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_LAYOUT_SINK (msctf/context.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_EXTENT
(msctf/range.c).
---
